=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 + the non-AI baseline:

(I3 baseline intact)
  The deterministic /api/v1/analytics/cost-forecast handler is unchanged
  in observable behaviour. Its SQL + math were extracted into a new
  package-level api.ComputeCostForecast helper that BOTH the existing
  GET handler AND the new AICostForecaster adapter call. The wire-shape
  response (costForecastResponse) is unchanged; only a new
  CostForecastMeta struct (private to the api package, exported for the
  adapter's consumption) was added with the analytic metadata the AI
  narrator needs. The chart on /cost-analysis renders identical numbers
  before and after this slice.

  The CostAnalysisPage adds the AI surface ABOVE CostForecastSection
  (gated by withAiFeature so it is absent in off mode). Every other
  baseline section (CostSummaryCards, MonthlyCostChart, CostPerKwhChart,
  ChargerTypeBreakdown, SavingsCalculator, MonthlyCostTable,
  TimeOfUseAnalysis, CostForecastSection, LifetimeSummary,
  EnvironmentalImpact) is rendered unchanged.

(I5 hidden UI)
  AICostForecastNarration is wrapped by withAiFeature('cost-forecast-
  narration', InnerSection). withAiFeature returns null when the feature
  is not enabled, so the entire DOM subtree is absent in off mode — no
  greyed-out button, no placeholder copy, no test-id stub. The off-mode
  React test asserts BOTH `container.toBeEmptyDOMElement()` AND the
  test-id is `not.toBeInTheDocument()`.

(I6 404 routes)
  POST /api/v1/ai/charging/costs/forecast/narrate is mounted via
  guard.Wrap("cost-forecast-narration", …) inside mountAIRoutes. The
  guard runs BEFORE the inner handler — when ai_mode='off' OR the
  per-feature toggle is off, it short-circuits to 404 and emits chi's
  "404 page not found\n" body. The Go off-mode test asserts the 404
  body does NOT leak the feature ID, the words "feature", "strategy",
  "provider", "agent", or any identifier that would reveal the AI
  surface exists.

(I7 per-feature)
  Every entry-point — backend route guard, frontend HOC, dispatcher
  resolution — keys on the literal feature ID "cost-forecast-narration".
  The off-mode tests intentionally set the toggle to true with mode='off'
  to prove mode trumps the toggle.

(I9 redaction)
  PolicyCostForecastNarration() in internal/ai/redact/policies.go
  declares Allow=ClassVehicleName + Mode=ModeRedactedTags. Cost data is
  aggregate dollar amounts and user-visible currency, so no class beyond
  vehicle name needs to be allowed; lat/long, addresses, and place names
  stay tagged on round-trip. The strategy's RedactionPolicy() returns
  this policy, so dispatch.Run installs it on every provider call.

(I10 type system)
  The AI surface lives entirely under /api/v1/ai/* with its own typed
  envelope ([tools.CostForecast]). The baseline /api/v1/analytics/cost-
  forecast wire-shape (costForecastResponse) is untouched; the
  CostForecastMeta fields are private to the AI envelope and never leak
  into the baseline response.

(I12 client/bg)
  No new background jobs, no new push kinds, no new client storage keys.
  One new SPA chunk ('ai-cost-forecast-narration') is implicit via the
  AICostForecastNarration component import on CostAnalysisPage; this is
  documented in the slice prompt's Off-mode contract impact section.

W1 inline wiring (P11 wired-or-absent + P12 no-placeholder-buttons):
  AICostForecastNarration imports useAiStream, computes the disabled
  prop from canGenerate (NOT a literal disabled), POSTs to the
  registered backend route /ai/charging/costs/forecast/narrate, double-
  submit-guards while streaming, and renders the SSE delta stream into
  the shared AiOutputPanel. The on-mode wiring test asserts (1) exactly
  one POST against the registered route, (2) the request body shape,
  (3) the first delta renders inside the gated wrapper, (4) the
  double-submit guard, and (5) computed-disabled when no vehicleId.

Why a SHARED ComputeCostForecast helper (rubber-duck blocking finding):
  Duplicating the cost-forecast SQL + math in the AICostForecaster
  adapter would mean (a) the AI narrator could quote different numbers
  than the chart renders, breaking I3, and (b) future tuning of the
  forecast (e.g. seasonal-adjustment weights, regression window) would
  have to be applied in two places. The refactor is the canonical fix
  the methodology recommends; both call sites consume the SAME
  deterministic computation.

Why an AICostForecaster adapter (not direct repo access from tools):
  internal/ai/tools/* is package-isolated to avoid circular imports with
  internal/database. The CostForecaster port (in tools/) is implemented
  by AICostForecaster in api/ which holds the *database.DB and delegates
  to the package-level api.ComputeCostForecast helper. Mirrors the
  AIBatteryHealthForecaster pattern from slice 0027.


